c", "author": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "No transaction or statement multiplexing; route chosen at login, never moves endpoint; replica profiles have no primary fallback", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null}, {"id": "claude_scope_003_build_state", "label": "CLAUDE.md: the repository also holds the scope 003 build: crates/pool-control, and the cluster, node and identity keys in pool-config", "_origin": "semantic", "author": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null}, {"id": "claude_cargo_deny_tool_install", "label": "deny needs cargo-deny 0.20.2, installed under target/tools by scripts/check.sh tools", "_origin": "semantic", "author": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null}, {"id": "claude_current_state", "label": "Current state: the planning package, the scope 001 workspace (apps/pool, the pool binary, and crates/pool-config), the scope 002 checks and the scope 003 build; the only product command is the offline pool check-config; no listener or proxy path yet; Rust 1.100.0 pinned by rust-toolchain.toml", "_origin": "semantic", "author": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null}, {"id": "claude_linux_build_note", "label": "linux-build and prove-checks --with-linux-build need a running Docker daemon; a macOS build is not Linux evidence; the evidence is in the verification records of spec 0001 and spec 0002", "_origin": "semantic", "author": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null}, {"id": "claude_next_feature_2", "label": "Features 1, 2 and 3 are done; their evidence is in the verification records of spec 0001, spec 0002 and spec 0003; the next queued feature is 4, the first walking slice whose acceptance is in docs/testing/strategy.md", "_origin": "semantic", "author": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null}, {"id": "claude_planned_commands", "label": "Commands, each check one command and the same that CI (.github/workflows/ci.yml) runs: scripts/check.sh all (fmt, clippy, test, deny, guards, docs), scripts/check.sh <name> (plus linux-build, fuzz, sbom, tools), scripts/prove-checks.sh, a single cargo test, the repo-check tests, check-config on valid-minimal.toml", "_origin": "semantic", "author": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null}, {"id": "claude_working_with_the_docs", "label": "Working with the Docs", "_origin": "semantic", "author": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null}, {"id": "claude", "label": "Claude Code guidance (CLAUDE.md)", "_origin": "semantic", "author": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "file_type": "document", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null}, {"id": "claude_agents_is_the_canonical_guide", "label": "CLAUDE.md points at AGENTS.md as the canonical agent guide (workflow, invariants, documentation ownership) and only adds what that guide does not cover; shared guidance is updated there, not in CLAUDE.md", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "_origin": "semantic"}, {"id": "claude_shape", "label": "Shape (CLAUDE.md): one Rust daemon (apps/pool) plus a separate admin CLI (apps/pool-cli) and four internal crates: pool-protocol and pool-config depend on no other POOL crate, pool-core depends on protocol and config, pool-control depends on config only", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "_origin": "semantic"}, {"id": "claude_core_and_control_never_depend_on_each_other", "label": "Core and control never depend on each other (CLAUDE.md): each owns its boundary types, the daemon maps control topology snapshots into core's route view, the CLI talks only to the versioned admin API, and there is no common crate", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Auth, pooling, router, balancer, health, failover and similar candidates start as modules inside core or control and are extracted only with a documented decision", "_origin": "semantic"}, {"id": "claude_safety_contracts_pointer", "label": "CLAUDE.md: the ten numbered safety contracts in spec 0001 are the detailed form of the AGENTS.md invariants; read them before touching leases, routing, cancellation or promotion", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "_origin": "semantic"}, {"id": "claude_work_queue", "label": "CLAUDE.md: docs/scope/index.md is the work queue with 17 features, the last 6 deferred; a status change must update both the index row and the feature file's heading; feature numbers are stable across renames", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "_origin": "semantic"}, {"id": "claude_feature_steps_as_slash_commands", "label": "CLAUDE.md: feature files list their steps as slash commands (/architect, /develop, /check verify, /test, /check review, /document) that co